gridcoinresearch (5.5.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  The testnet daemon's systemd units are new in this release. Existing service
  setups were switched over to them during this upgrade; this is what changed.

  The system service runs as the account gridcointestnet. systemd hands
  /var/lib/gridcointestnetd to the new account at the service's first start, and /etc/gridcoin-testnet is
  now root:gridcointestnet 0710. A /etc/gridcoin-testnet/gridcoin.conf owned
  by root is given the group gridcointestnet and made readable by that group
  only; one owned by gridcoin must be given to root:gridcointestnet, mode 0640,
  by hand. A missing one is created as root:gridcointestnet 0640 with
  generated RPC credentials.

  The units are Type=notify: the core reports to systemd itself when it is
  ready, with no forking and no pid file. The units pass -nodaemon and
  -nodaemonwait, so daemon=1 or daemonwait=1 in a configuration file no longer
  matters.

  Autounlock moved to a socket-activated helper:
  gridcointestnet-autounlock.socket for the system service, and
  gridcointestnet-autounlock@<user>.socket for a per-user core. The core asks
  the helper for the passphrase. Enabled autounlock setups were switched over
  automatically. No credential was decrypted, re-encrypted or moved: a
  per-user credential stays in /etc/credstore.encrypted.

  The old unit gridcointestnetd-autounlock@.service and its RPC helper script
  are removed. Its instances were disabled and stopped before the upgrade.

  A desktop user attaches the GUI to the system service through membership of
  the gridcointestnet-gui group ("Connect to the system service" in the
  menu). A new membership takes effect at the user's next login.

  A per-user core now needs "gridcointestnet-service enable-user <user>"
  before it starts: "systemctl enable gridcointestnetd@<user>" alone gives an
  instance that stops with exit status 78 and says so. Instances that were
  enabled or running were set up during the upgrade, with the datadir they
  used, and running ones were restarted without waiting for them.

  Drop-ins of the old per-user unit (from "systemctl edit
  gridcointestnetd@<user>") were renamed to
  <name>.disabled-by-gridcoin-switchover, so that their settings, written for a
  forking daemon, no longer apply. A -datadir set in one was kept. Review them
  and put back with "systemctl edit" what still applies.

  Ubuntu 22.04 builds have no autounlock (it needs systemd 251 or later): the
  old autounlock units were turned off there, and the cores start with the
  wallet locked.

  If the switch-over did not finish for a user, the upgrade said why, and
  /var/lib/gridcoin-service/switchover-test.state keeps what is left. Fix the
  cause and run "gridcointestnet-service switch-over
  --state=/var/lib/gridcoin-service/switchover-test.state". Until then that
  user's core is not restarted, and once stopped it may not start again.

  The full description is in doc/running-unattended.md.

 -- Gridcoin Developers <dev@gridcoin.us>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
